# Normalise line endings.
#
# The working tree is CRLF but every blob in HEAD is LF, so without this git
# reports all 256 tracked files as modified and any `git add -A` sweeps a
# whitespace-only rewrite of the whole repo into the commit.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` makes git normalise to LF on the way into the index and
# leave the working tree alone. CRLF files then compare equal to their LF blobs
# and drop out of `git status` on their own — no renormalise commit needed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Keep these exactly as they are on disk.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.blueprint binary
*.customBattle -text
